---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageMeta from '@/components/PageMeta.astro';
import JourneyNav from '@/components/ia/JourneyNav.astro';
---

<Layout title="Validation, conformance and generated projections" description="How SPDTF 2.0 separates deterministic checks, semantic review, lifecycle records and generated delivery views.">
  <PageMeta category="Ontology journey" variant="brand" updated="SPDTF 2.0 development · assurance and projections" />
  <h1>Validation, conformance, lifecycle and generated projections</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Validation makes encoded checks visible. Conformance states which features and tests
    were exercised. Neither one is semantic approval: practitioners review meaning and
    governance records any promotion.
  </p>
  <JourneyNav />

  <h2 id="separate">Keep the decisions separate</h2>
  <table>
    <caption>Different checks answer different questions</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Layer</th><th scope="col">Question</th><th scope="col">Evidence</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Semantic review</th><td>Does this definition, relationship or boundary match the group’s domain meaning?</td><td>Participant evidence, examples, questions, review comments and disposition.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Deterministic validation</th><td>Does the candidate satisfy the encoded structural, provenance, coverage and constraint checks?</td><td>Fail-closed reports, SHACL scope, parser results and reproducible receipts.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Conformance</th><td>Which exact standards features and profiles were tested?</td><td>Version, feature declaration, test suite and known non-claims.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Governance promotion</th><td>Who may make the decision, and was it recorded?</td><td>Decision record, authority, lifecycle state and immutable release identifier.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="lifecycle">Candidate lifecycle</h2>
  <p>
    The current vocabulary ceiling is <strong>first working-group draft — non-normative</strong>
    until a separately accepted governance decision defines later promotion states. A
    candidate can be revised, deferred or returned for evidence without being described
    as an adopted standard.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Publish a readable candidate with sources, questions, status and change history.</li>
    <li>Run the declared validation and conformance checks; record their exact scope.</li>
    <li>Review feedback and record accepted, needs evidence, deferred or not accepted dispositions.</li>
    <li>Preserve the immutable diff and receipts; only recorded human authority can promote a release.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="projections">Generated projections</h2>
  <p>
    A governed semantic package may produce RDF/OWL/SKOS, SHACL constraints, JSON Schema,
    JSON-LD contexts, forms, APIs, website pages, PDF and Markdown. These are tested
    projections for different consumers, not independent specifications. An optional
    transformation runtime is an implementation service, not a source of meaning.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/spdtf-2">Return to SPDTF 2.0 Development</a> ·
    <a href="/pdtf-1">Compare with the retained PDTF 1.0 implementation</a>
  </p>
</Layout>
